| `text-align` | Aligns text horizontally |
| `align-items` | Aligns items on the cross axis |
| `border` | Adds a border on all four sides |
| `border-bottom` | Adds a border only at the bottom |
| `inherit` | Makes a property take its value from the parent |
| `flex-direction` | Defines the direction of Flexbox items |

## Conclusion

CSS helps us control the appearance and layout of web elements. Understanding text alignment, inheritance, borders, and Flexbox alignment makes it easier to design webpages and solve styling problems.

These concepts are useful when creating business cards, navigation bars, forms, buttons, and other web layouts.
